chromium-embedded-framework for Debian
======================================

This package uses Multiple Upstream Tarballs (MUT) format with 3.0 (quilt)
source format. All source components are distributed as separate tarballs.

================================================================================
SOURCE PACKAGE STRUCTURE (MUT)
================================================================================

The source package consists of 4 tarballs:

    chromium-embedded-framework_VERSION.orig.tar.xz
        CEF source code (main upstream tarball)

    chromium-embedded-framework_VERSION.orig-chromium.tar.xz
        Chromium browser source (from Debian chromium package)

    chromium-embedded-framework_VERSION.orig-depot-tools.tar.xz
        Google's depot_tools build system

    chromium-embedded-framework_VERSION.orig-rust.tar.xz
        Rust standard library sources (interim bundled dependency)

When extracted with dpkg-source -x, these create:

    chromium-embedded-framework-VERSION/
    ├── cef/                    <- CEF source (from orig.tar.xz)
    ├── chromium/               <- From orig-chromium.tar.xz
    ├── depot-tools/            <- From orig-depot-tools.tar.xz (note: hyphen)
    ├── rust/                   <- From orig-rust.tar.xz
    └── debian/                 <- Packaging files

NOTE: MUT component names use HYPHENS (depot-tools), not underscores.
The main tarball contains CEF source in a cef/ subdirectory.

================================================================================
BUILD INSTRUCTIONS
================================================================================

Standard Build (from source package):

    $ dpkg-source -x chromium-embedded-framework_*.dsc
    $ cd chromium-embedded-framework-*/
    $ dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc

The MUT components are automatically extracted by dpkg-source -x.

Build Time: ~7+ hours (depends on hardware)
Disk Space: ~40 GB required

================================================================================
COMPONENT TARBALLS
================================================================================

1. CEF Source (orig.tar.xz)
---------------------------
Obtained from: https://bitbucket.org/chromiumembedded/cef
Branch: Must match Chromium's build number (e.g., branch 7499 for Chromium 143.x)

2. Chromium Source (orig-chromium.tar.xz)
-----------------------------------------
Obtained from: Debian chromium package source
Command: apt-get source --download-only chromium
Rename: mv chromium_*.orig.tar.xz chromium-embedded-framework_VERSION.orig-chromium.tar.xz

3. depot-tools (orig-depot-tools.tar.xz)
----------------------------------------
Obtained from: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git
This tarball is cleaned of binary files (.cipd*, *.exe, *.dll, etc.)

4. Rust Standard Library (orig-rust.tar.xz)
-------------------------------------------
Interim bundled dependency. Required because Debian rust-src is missing files
that Chromium's build system expects (sync/nonpoison/condvar.rs, rwlock.rs).

This component can be removed when Debian rust-src catches up to Chromium's
expected Rust version.

================================================================================
DESIGN DECISIONS
================================================================================

1. WHY FULL CHROMIUM SOURCE (not just headers)
----------------------------------------------
CEF uses internal Chromium APIs, not just the public API. For example:

- CEF includes 43+ headers from content/browser/ (internal implementation)
  rather than content/public/browser/ (stable public API)
- libcef/browser/browser_host_base.cc includes internal headers like
  content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.h
- CEF's off-screen rendering extends content::RenderWidgetHostViewBase
  from content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_base.h

These internal classes don't have stable ABIs and their implementation can
change between Chromium versions. CEF hooks into Chromium's internal browser
infrastructure, requiring source-level integration with a matching Chromium
version. A headers-only approach (chromium-headers package) would not work
because the ninja build targets depend on compiled Chromium object files.

2. WHY DEPOT_TOOLS IS BUNDLED
-----------------------------
depot_tools is Google's build infrastructure for Chromium-based projects.
CEF's automate-git.py script expects depot_tools for:
- gclient: Dependency management and configuration
- gn: Build file generation
- autoninja: Parallel compilation wrapper

NETWORK ISOLATION: This package does NOT access the internet during build.
- Patch 0003-network-isolation-disable-google-storage-downloads makes
  download_from_google_storage.py a no-op
- The --no-depot-tools-update flag prevents upstream pulls
- All source is bundled in the MUT tarballs

The git clone commands in debian/rules error messages only explain how to
obtain depot_tools if missing - they don't execute during normal builds.

3. LOCAL GIT INITIALIZATION
---------------------------
debian/rules creates local git repositories with git init && git commit.
This satisfies CEF's automate-git.py which expects git repositories for
source directories. This is completely network-free but unusual for Debian.

A cleaner approach would be patching automate-git.py to remove git
requirements entirely, though the necessary changes would be complex
for limited benefit.

================================================================================
CONFIGURATION DECISIONS
================================================================================

1. SYSTEM LIBC++ (use_custom_libcxx=false)
------------------------------------------
Uses Debian's libc++-19-dev instead of bundled libc++.
Aligns with Debian Chromium's approach.

2. SYSTEM LLVM/CLANG (clang-19)
-------------------------------
Uses Debian's clang-19 toolchain. No bundled compiler.

3. SYSTEM FFMPEG (is_component_ffmpeg=true)
-------------------------------------------
Uses system FFmpeg for media codecs.
Enables H.264/AAC when user installs libavcodec-extra.

================================================================================
PATCHES
================================================================================

CEF Patches (debian/patches/*.cef.patch)
----------------------------------------
Applied via quilt during dpkg-source extraction.
Patch paths have cef/ prefix (e.g., cef/tools/automate/automate-git.py).
See debian/patches/series for the order.

Chromium Patches (debian/patches/chromium/*.chromium.patch)
-----------------------------------------------------------
Applied manually via patch -p1 in debian/rules.
These patches modify Chromium source, not CEF source.

================================================================================
MAINTENANCE
================================================================================

Updating CEF Version:
1. Update CEF source in orig.tar.xz
2. Update CEF_BRANCH in debian/rules
3. Update chromium version to match CEF requirements
4. Regenerate orig-chromium.tar.xz from new Debian chromium
5. Test build and fix any patch conflicts

Updating Chromium Version:
1. apt-get source --download-only chromium
2. Rename and replace orig-chromium.tar.xz
3. Test build and fix patch conflicts

Updating LLVM Version:
1. Update Build-Depends in debian/control
2. Update CLANG_MVERS in debian/rules
3. Update patch 0012-bindgen-libclang-abspath.chromium.patch

